{
  "summary": "P1 lost laptop. Mei Chen (user_id 9, Operations, Logistics Analyst, Chicago). Reports leaving work laptop BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15) in an Uber last night; she doesn't know if it was locked. Device status: ONLINE NOW, last check-in 2026-10-09T14:04:38Z, no warnings, 512GB disk with 437GB used. So someone may have it powered on and connected. Likely data on it: Operations/logistics files, saved M365 (mailbox is 99.4% full, ~50GB, may be cached locally) and VPN sessions. Sign-in logs (14 days): 9 successful sign-ins, all Chicago, corporate/home residential IPs, Duo push, during usual hours; none since 2026-10-08 13:23Z; no failures or hosting networks. Account active, not blocked. Queued block_sign_in (approval id 1, pending tech approval). Needed: remote lock/wipe of BL-LT-0109 while it's online, revoke sessions/tokens, verify user identity and plan a password reset afterward, issue a loaner device. User has been asked for the timeline, ride details, and to contact Uber lost-and-found and file a police report if it isn't recovered.",
  "reason": "KB-021 says always escalate for remote lock/wipe; P1"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Mei, thanks for telling us so quickly. We're treating this as urgent. Here's where things stand: (1) We've asked for your account to be blocked so nobody can use sessions saved on that laptop. A technician has to approve this first, and once they do, you won't be able to sign in to email, Teams or VPN until we confirm it's you and set you up with a new password. That password will be given to you by phone, never by email. (2) We've handed this to our senior team so they can remotely lock or wipe the laptop. To help us, please reply with: roughly when and where you last had it, the time and route of the Uber ride, and whether the laptop was asleep, shut, or open when you left it. Please also report it through the Uber app's lost items feature. If it isn't found, please file a police report and send us the report number. We'll be in touch shortly about getting you a loaner laptop.",
  "internal_note": "KB-021 followed. User 9, device BL-LT-0109 (macOS 15): ONLINE, last check-in 2026-10-09T14:04:38Z, so it may be powered on in someone else's hands. Lock state is unknown. Sign-in logs over 14 days are clean: 9 successful sign-ins, all Chicago, corporate or home IPs, Duo push, within usual hours, none after 2026-10-08 13:23Z, no failures. Queued block_sign_in (approval id 1), pending tech approval. Escalated to Tier 2 (escalation id 1) for remote lock/wipe while the device is online, session/token revocation, a password reset after identity verification, and a loaner. Mailbox is 99.4% full and may be cached on the device. Still waiting on the user's timeline and ride details.",
